  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;The proposed two-storey side extension, by reason of its bulk, massing and design, would present a discordant feature with a disjointed roofline that also results in an overdevelopment of the modest semi-detached dwelling, when in combination with the existing two-storey side extension. Furthermore, it would compromise the openness between the application site and no.13 Vicar&#x27;s Walk, consequently diminishing the distinction between the two buildings. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif&quot;&gt;For these reasons, the proposal would appear at odds with the established character and appearance of the surrounding area, which is particularly notable given its location within the Becontree Estate non-designated heritage asset.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;As such, the proposed development is contrary to: - National Planning Policy Framework&amp;nbsp; National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024);&amp;nbsp; -Policies D1, D4, D5, D6 and HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021)&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-Policies DMD1, DMD4, DMD5 and SP2 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024); and&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (February 2012).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
